#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use this composable, explicit execution model with your utility-scale experiments to fine-tune error mitigation and other techniques."
msgstr "Gamitin ang composable, explicit na execution model na ito sa iyong mga utility-scale na eksperimento para i-fine-tune ang error mitigation at iba pang mga teknik."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Directed execution model (beta)"
msgstr "Directed execution model (beta)"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Directed execution model (beta) {#directed-execution-model-beta}"
msgstr "Directed execution model (beta) {#directed-execution-model-beta}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Beta release\">\n"
"All components in the directed execution model are currently in beta and might not be stable. You are invited to test them and provide feedback by opening an issue in the [Samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic/issues) or [Qiskit Runtime](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/issues) GitHub repositories.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Beta release\">\n"
"Lahat ng mga komponente sa directed execution model ay kasalukuyang nasa beta at maaaring hindi pa stable. Inaanyayahan kang subukan ang mga ito at magbigay ng feedback sa pamamagitan ng pagbubukas ng isyu sa [Samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic/issues) o [Qiskit Runtime](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/issues) na mga GitHub repository.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampler and Estimator primitive interfaces provide a higher-level abstraction for algorithm developers to focus more on innovation and less on data conversion. However, they are less suitable for quantum information scientists, who require more control and flexibility for their utility-scale experiments. The **directed execution model**, currently in beta release, addresses this need. This execution model provides the ingredients to capture design intents on the client side, and shifts the costly generation of circuit variants to the server side, so that you can fine-tune error mitigation and other techniques without sacrificing performance. This explicit and composable model makes it easier to experiment with new techniques, reproduce results, and share methods.\n"
msgstr "Ang Sampler at Estimator primitive na mga interface ay nagbibigay ng mas mataas na antas ng abstraction para sa mga developer ng algorithm upang mas makapag-focus sa inobasyon at hindi sa conversion ng data. Gayunpaman, hindi sila gaanong angkop para sa mga quantum information scientist, na nangangailangan ng mas maraming kontrol at flexibility para sa kanilang mga utility-scale na eksperimento. Ang **directed execution model**, na kasalukuyang nasa beta release, ay tumutugon sa pangangailangang ito. Ang execution model na ito ay nagbibigay ng mga sangkap para ma-capture ang mga design intent sa client side, at inililipat ang mahal na paglikha ng mga variant ng circuit sa server side, upang maaari kang mag-fine-tune ng error mitigation at iba pang mga teknik nang hindi sinasacrifice ang performance. Ang explicit at composable na model na ito ay nagpapadali ng pag-eksperimento sa mga bagong teknik, pagpaparami ng mga resulta, at pagbabahagi ng mga pamamaraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In its beta release, the directed execution model focuses on giving you control over techniques that are built into the existing Sampler and Estimator, including Pauli twirling, noise model learning and injection, and basis changes. Support for other capabilities will be added gradually over time.\n"
msgstr "Sa beta release nito, ang directed execution model ay nakatuon sa pagbibigay sa iyo ng kontrol sa mga teknik na built-in na sa kasalukuyang Sampler at Estimator, kabilang ang Pauli twirling, noise model learning at injection, at mga pagbabago ng basis. Ang suporta para sa iba pang mga kakayahan ay unti-unting idadagdag sa paglipas ng panahon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow {#workflow}"
msgstr "Workflow {#workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One main goal of the directed execution model is to provide a modular way to apply error mitigation methods. For example, you can define which layers in the circuit to mitigate, or adjust the noise rates being injected into the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang isa sa mga pangunahing layunin ng directed execution model ay magbigay ng modular na paraan para mag-apply ng mga paraan ng error mitigation. Halimbawa, maaari mong tukuyin kung aling mga layer sa circuit ang dapat pagaanin, o ayusin ang mga noise rate na ini-inject sa circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To apply error mitigation to a circuit under the framework, your workflow will typically involve the following steps (the tools mentioned here are described more fully in the [next section](#samplomatic-tools)):\n"
msgstr "Para mag-apply ng error mitigation sa isang circuit sa ilalim ng framework, ang iyong workflow ay karaniwang magsasangkot ng mga sumusunod na hakbang (ang mga tool na nabanggit dito ay mas buong inilalarawan sa [susunod na seksyon](#samplomatic-tools)):\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group instructions into boxes and apply annotations to them. The annotations capture the intended transformation without actually generating the circuit variants.\n"
msgstr "I-group ang mga instruksyon sa mga box at mag-apply ng mga annotation sa mga ito. Kino-capture ng mga annotation ang nilalayon na transformation nang hindi aktwal na gumagawa ng mga variant ng circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    *If needed*: Learn the noise models of the unique layers using the new [NoiseLearnerV3](#noiselearnerv3). \n"
msgstr "    *Kung kinakailangan*: Aralin ang mga noise model ng mga natatanging layer gamit ang bagong [NoiseLearnerV3](#noiselearnerv3).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the template circuit and samplex from the boxed circuit.\n"
msgstr "Buuin ang template circuit at samplex mula sa boxed circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the template circuit and samplex with the [Executor](#executor) primitive, which will generate and execute the circuit variants as instructed. \n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang template circuit at samplex gamit ang [Executor](#executor) primitive, na lilikha at magpapatakbo ng mga variant ng circuit ayon sa instruksyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process execution results. For example, you can apply postselection, or extrapolate mitigated expectation values from the execution results.\n"
msgstr "I-post-process ang mga resulta ng execution. Halimbawa, maaari kang mag-apply ng postselection, o mag-extrapolate ng mga mitigated expectation value mula sa mga resulta ng execution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image illustrating the steps occurring on the client side and server side of the directed execution model](/docs/images/guides/directed-execution-model/dem.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Image illustrating the steps occurring on the client side and server side of the directed execution model](/docs/images/guides/directed-execution-model/dem.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"samplomatic-tools\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"samplomatic-tools\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tools for the directed execution model {#tools-for-the-directed-execution-model}"
msgstr "Mga tool para sa directed execution model {#tools-for-the-directed-execution-model}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following tools can be used together to implement an error mitigation technique in the directed execution model.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga sumusunod na tool ay maaaring gamitin nang magkasama para ipatupad ang isang teknik ng error mitigation sa directed execution model.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"samplomatic\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"samplomatic\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"
msgstr "Samplomatic {#samplomatic}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic/) is a new open-source library that supports customized sampling randomizations. It uses the [box](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#box) construct to reason about collections of circuit operations that should be treated as having a stable noise context, and uses annotations on boxes to allow you to declare and configure intents. For example, you can stratify your circuit into boxes, add a twirling annotation to each box, and specify which twirling group to use, as shown in the following figure:\n"
msgstr "Ang [Samplomatic](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic/) ay isang bagong open-source na library na sumusuporta sa mga customized sampling randomization. Gumagamit ito ng [box](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#box) na construct para pag-isipan ang mga koleksyon ng mga circuit operation na dapat tratuhin bilang may stable na noise context, at gumagamit ng mga annotation sa mga box para payagan kang mag-declare at mag-configure ng mga intent. Halimbawa, maaari mong stratify ang iyong circuit sa mga box, magdagdag ng twirling annotation sa bawat box, at tukuyin kung aling twirling group ang gagamitin, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod na figure:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Example of using boxes and twirling annotations](/docs/images/guides/directed-execution-model/execution-model.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Halimbawa ng paggamit ng mga box at twirling annotation](/docs/images/guides/directed-execution-model/execution-model.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A circuit with annotated boxes can then be used to generate a *template circuit* and a *samplex*. The output template circuit is a parameterized circuit that will be executed without further alteration (other than having different parameter values assigned to it). The samplex, which is the core type of the Samplomatic library, represents a parametric probability distribution over the parameters of the template circuit and other array-valued fields. These fields can be used to post-process data collected from executing the bound template circuit. In other words, the template circuit and samplex together tell the [Executor primitive](#executor) what parameters to generate and what bound circuits to run. Because these two constructs are created on the client side, you can do local inspection and sampling to verify the outputs prior to sending it for hardware execution. \n"
msgstr "Ang isang circuit na may mga annotated box ay maaaring gamitin para gumawa ng *template circuit* at *samplex*. Ang output template circuit ay isang parameterized circuit na isasagawa nang walang karagdagang pagbabago (maliban sa magkakaibang mga halaga ng parameter na itatalaga sa kanya). Ang samplex, na siyang pangunahing uri ng Samplomatic library, ay kumakatawan sa isang parametric probability distribution sa mga parameter ng template circuit at iba pang mga field na may array na halaga. Ang mga field na ito ay maaaring gamitin para i-post-process ang data na nakolekta mula sa pagpapatakbo ng bound template circuit. Sa madaling salita, ang template circuit at samplex nang magkasama ay nagsasabi sa [Executor primitive](#executor) kung aling mga parameter ang dapat likhain at kung aling mga bound circuit ang dapat patakbuhin. Dahil ang dalawang construct na ito ay nilikha sa client side, maaari kang gumawa ng lokal na inspeksyon at sampling para i-verify ang mga output bago ipadala para sa hardware execution.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To simplify the process of generating annotated boxes, the Samplomatic library also provides transpiler passes that automatically group circuit instructions into annotated boxes, based on the strategies you provide.\n"
msgstr "Para pasimplehin ang proseso ng paglikha ng mga annotated box, ang Samplomatic library ay nagbibigay din ng mga transpiler pass na awtomatikong nag-igroup ng mga instruksyon ng circuit sa mga annotated box, batay sa mga estratehiya na ibinibigay mo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To learn more about Samplomatic, visit the [guides](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/index.html) and [API reference](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/) documentation. Feel free to submit feedback and report bugs in its [GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) repository.\n"
msgstr "Para matuto pa tungkol sa Samplomatic, bisitahin ang [guides](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/index.html) at [API reference](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/) na dokumentasyon. Huwag mag-atubiling magpadala ng feedback at mag-ulat ng mga bug sa [GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/samplomatic) repository nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"executor\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"executor\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Executor primitive {#executor-primitive}"
msgstr "Executor primitive {#executor-primitive}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Executor is a new Qiskit Runtime primitive that takes the (template circuit, samplex) pair as input, generates and binds parameter values according to the samplex, executes the bound circuits on the hardware, and returns the execution results and metadata. It follows the directives of the input pair and does not make any implicit decisions for you, so that the process is transparent yet performant. \n"
msgid "Executor is a new IBM Quantum primitive that takes the (template circuit, samplex) pair as input, generates and binds parameter values according to the samplex, executes the bound circuits on the hardware, and returns the execution results and metadata. It follows the directives of the input pair and does not make any implicit decisions for you, so that the process is transparent yet performant. \n"
msgstr "Ang Executor ay isang bagong Qiskit Runtime primitive na tumatanggap ng pares na (template circuit, samplex) bilang input, gumagawa at nagbubuklod ng mga halaga ng parameter ayon sa samplex, nagpapatakbo ng mga bound circuit sa hardware, at nagbabalik ng mga resulta ng execution at metadata. Sinusunod nito ang mga direktibo ng input na pares at hindi gumagawa ng anumang implicit na desisyon para sa iyo, upang ang proseso ay transparent ngunit mahusay.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"
msgstr "NoiseLearnerV3 {#noiselearnerv3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Similar to the current [`NoiseLearner`](/guides/noise-learning), this Qiskit Runtime helper program returns the sparse [Pauli-Lindblad noise model](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866) that is used in many error mitigation methods, including [PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec), [PEA](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea), and [PNA](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-pna/tree/main). In the original `NoiseLearner`, you pass in a list of circuits, and the program stratifies the circuits into layers and returns the noise model for each unique layer. `NoiseLearnerV3`, on the other hand, gives you control over how to stratify your circuits, and the program simply takes a list of boxed circuit instructions (for example, unique layers) as the inputs. \n"
msgid "Similar to the current [`NoiseLearner`](/guides/noise-learning), this `qiskit-ibm-runtime` helper program returns the sparse [Pauli-Lindblad noise model](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866) that is used in many error mitigation methods, including [PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec), [PEA](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea), and [PNA](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-pna/tree/main). In the original `NoiseLearner`, you pass in a list of circuits, and the program stratifies the circuits into layers and returns the noise model for each unique layer. `NoiseLearnerV3`, on the other hand, gives you control over how to stratify your circuits, and the program simply takes a list of boxed circuit instructions (for example, unique layers) as the inputs. \n"
msgstr "Katulad ng kasalukuyang [`NoiseLearner`](/guides/noise-learning), ang Qiskit Runtime helper program na ito ay nagbabalik ng sparse na [Pauli-Lindblad noise model](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866) na ginagamit sa maraming paraan ng error mitigation, kabilang ang [PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec), [PEA](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#probabilistic-error-amplification-pea), at [PNA](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-pna/tree/main). Sa orihinal na `NoiseLearner`, nagpapasa ka ng listahan ng mga circuit, at ang programa ay nagla-layer ng mga circuit at nagbabalik ng noise model para sa bawat natatanging layer. Ang `NoiseLearnerV3`, sa kabilang banda, ay nagbibigay sa iyo ng kontrol sa kung paano i-stratify ang iyong mga circuit, at ang programa ay simpleng tumatanggap ng listahan ng mga boxed circuit instruction (halimbawa, mga natatanging layer) bilang mga input.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearnerV3` also supports measurement noise learning. For each instruction set in the input list, it runs the Pauli-Lindblad learning protocol if the set contains one- and two-qubit gates, and the [TREX](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex) protocol if the set contains measurements.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuportahan din ng `NoiseLearnerV3` ang measurement noise learning. Para sa bawat instruction set sa listahan ng input, pinapatakbo nito ang Pauli-Lindblad learning protocol kung ang set ay naglalaman ng isa- at dalawang-qubit gate, at ang [TREX](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex) protocol kung ang set ay naglalaman ng mga measurement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearnerV3` was released with [`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.47.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes#0470-2026-05-12). To learn more, see the [Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning#noiselearnerv3) guide, and refer to its [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-v3-noise-learner-v3) documentation.\n"
msgstr "Inilabas ang `NoiseLearnerV3` kasama ang [`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.47.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes#0470-2026-05-12). Para matuto pa, tingnan ang gabay na [Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning#noiselearnerv3), at tingnan ang [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/noise-learner-v3-noise-learner-v3) na dokumentasyon nito.\n"

